{{-- Refund & Cancellation Policy — English master version. --}}
<p>This policy explains how cancellations and refunds work for paid products of {{ $legal['name'] }} (GameCon+, the GameCon+ family plan, GameCon+ gifts and server promotion).</p>

<h2>1. Merchant of Record — Paddle</h2>
<p>Our order process is conducted by our online reseller <strong>Paddle.com</strong>. <strong>Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record</strong> for all our orders: it processes payments, charges applicable taxes, issues receipts and invoices, and handles refunds and payment-related customer service. Refunds are paid back by Paddle to the original payment method.</p>

<h2>2. Digital subscription with instant access</h2>
<p>GameCon+ is a digital software-as-a-service subscription. Access to the paid features is activated <strong>immediately</strong> after a successful payment (usually within a few seconds) and is available in your account on the website and in the app. Gifts are delivered to the recipient’s account immediately; server promotion starts immediately or, if all paid slots are taken, at the first free slot shown before payment.</p>

<h2>3. Cancellation</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>One click.</strong> You can cancel a subscription at any time on the GameCon+ page of your profile (button “Cancel”). You can also cancel via the link in your Paddle receipt or by writing to us.</li>
    <li><strong>No hidden fees.</strong> There are no cancellation fees, penalties or minimum terms.</li>
    <li><strong>Access until the end of the paid period.</strong> After cancellation the subscription will not renew; GameCon+ stays active until the end of the period you already paid for. Until then you can resume the subscription in one click.</li>
    <li>Deleting your account cancels active subscriptions.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Refunds</h2>
<h3>4.1. 14-day refund window</h3>
<p>You may request a full refund within <strong>14 days of the initial payment</strong> for a new subscription, a gift or a server promotion. This follows the consumer standard of the EU, the UK and the US. By purchasing, you request immediate access to the digital service; where the law requires it, you acknowledge that you may lose a statutory right of withdrawal once the service has been fully provided — however, we still honour the 14-day refund window described here as a goodwill policy, subject to section 4.4.</p>
<h3>4.2. Renewals</h3>
<p>Automatic renewal payments are generally non-refundable, because you can cancel before renewal at any time. If you forgot to cancel and have not used the paid features since the renewal, contact us within 14 days of the renewal and we will consider a refund.</p>
<h3>4.3. Technical issues and duplicate charges</h3>
<ul>
    <li>If you were charged twice for the same product or period, or charged after a confirmed cancellation, we will refund the duplicate or erroneous amount in full, regardless of the time limits above.</li>
    <li>If paid features did not work because of a fault on our side and we could not fix it within a reasonable time, we will refund the affected period in full or pro rata.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.4. Limitations and abuse</h3>
<ul>
    <li>We may refuse a refund where there is evidence of abuse, for example repeated purchase-and-refund cycles, refunds requested after substantial use of a gift or promotion, use of the refund window to obtain paid features for free, fraud, or chargebacks filed while a refund request is open.</li>
    <li>No refund is due if your account was suspended or terminated for a serious breach of our <a href="{{ $legal['site'] }}/terms">Terms of Service</a>, unless the law requires otherwise.</li>
    <li>Changes to the list of paid features (see Terms, section 7) do not by themselves give a right to a refund, except where required by applicable consumer law.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing in this policy limits your mandatory statutory rights as a consumer.</p>

<h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Use the link in the receipt e-mail from Paddle, or find your order at <a href="https://paddle.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener">paddle.net</a>; or</li>
    <li>write to <a href="mailto:{{ $legal['email'] }}">{{ $legal['email'] }}</a> with the e-mail used for the purchase, the order number (from the receipt) and the reason.</li>
</ol>
<p>We aim to respond within 3 business days. Approved refunds are processed by Paddle to the original payment method; the time for funds to appear depends on your bank (usually 5–10 business days). After a refund, the related paid access (subscription, gift or promotion) ends.</p>

<h2>6. Chargebacks</h2>
<p>Please contact us before disputing a payment with your bank — most issues are solved faster directly. Accounts with unjustified chargebacks may lose paid access.</p>

<h2>7. Contact</h2>
<p>{{ $legal['operator'] }} — <a href="mailto:{{ $legal['email'] }}">{{ $legal['email'] }}</a>.</p>
